<title>CHINA: Coal mine accident kills 31 in east China.</title>
<headline>Coal mine accident kills 31 in east China.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A gas explosion at a coal mine in eastern China has killed 31 miners, state radio said on Monday.</p>
<p>The explosion occurred last Friday at the Nanxiye coal mine in Laiwu in eastern Shandong province, the radio said but gave no reason for the delay in reporting the disaster.</p>
<p>A total of 31 people were killed, it said and blamed the explosion on the mine's ventilation system, which was below standard. It gave no more details.</p>
<p>China has issued a string of directives to improve safety in its mines with explosions and accidents, mainly at improperly maintained village level mines, killing up to 10,000 miners each year.</p>
</text>
